{"format":1,"key":"zone:feralas","path":"/lore/zone/feralas","name":"Feralas","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"feralas","name":"Feralas","path":"/lore/zone/feralas"},"levels":"","description":"Feralas is a vast, mist-shrouded rainforest nestled between Desolace, Thousand Needles, and the Veiled Sea. Sheltered by soaring mountain walls, it…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:feralas","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Feralas is a vast, mist-shrouded rainforest nestled between Desolace, Thousand Needles, and the Veiled Sea. Sheltered by soaring mountain walls, it preserves an ancient ecosystem dotted with overgrown Kaldorei ruins and primordial beasts. Today, the wilderness is contested territory, caught between ancient Highborne remnants, invasive Gordunni ogres, and rival outposts established by the Alliance and the Horde.","While neighboring Desolace and Thousand Needles have dried into barren badlands and desiccated canyons, Feralas remains intensely verdant. Mountain ranges seal off the canopy, sustaining a warm microclimate of deep mists, ancient trees, and towering waterfalls. Before the Great Sundering, much of Kalimdor looked like this. Over millennia, the deep jungle swallowed the monuments of the Kaldorei civilization that once ruled here, hiding forgotten temples and pavilions beneath strangling moss and thick fern brush.","Dominating central Feralas is the ruined metropolis of Eldre'Thalas, now called Dire Maul. Built at the peak of the Kaldorei empire, its vast stone courtyards have fallen into ruin, desecrated by the savage Gordunni ogre clan. These ogres spread across the valley, pillaging sacred sites, defiling pristine groves, and driving indigenous wildlife into territorial frenzy. Deep within Dire Maul's sealed chambers, whispers persist of Highborne remnants and trapped powers dating back ten thousand years.","Both the Alliance and the Horde have mounted major expeditions into the jungle, though traversing it remains dangerous. From Feathermoon Stronghold on Sardor Isle, General Shandris Feathermoon directs Sentinels against both ogre expansion and encroaching naga. To the east lies Camp Mojache, a central Horde garrison struggling against aggressive Woodpaw gnolls, hostile Grimtotem tauren, and the relentless ogre clans. Neither faction commands true control over the untamable interior."],"hash":"aca08d","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"585e071fc1","sec":119},"female-narrator":{"sha":"e2a426d86e","sec":124}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Feralas (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Feralas_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Feralas","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Feralas"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/dire-maul","n":"Dire Maul","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/feathermoon-stronghold","n":"Feathermoon Stronghold","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/camp-mojache","n":"Camp Mojache","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/thalanaar","n":"Thalanaar","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dream-bough","n":"Dream Bough","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/forgotten-coast","n":"Forgotten Coast","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/twin-colossals","n":"Twin Colossals","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/thousandneedles","n":"Thousand Needles","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/twilight-grove","n":"Twilight Grove","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/3116-simple-sigil","n":"Simple Sigil","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/item/simple-sigil","n":"Simple Sigil","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1059-reclaiming-the-charred-vale","n":"Reclaiming the Charred Vale","k":"quest"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/camp-mojache","n":"Camp Mojache","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/capital-gardens","n":"Capital Gardens","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dire-maul","n":"Dire Maul","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/dream-bough","n":"Dream Bough","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/eldreth-row","n":"Eldreth Row","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/feathermoon-stronghold","n":"Feathermoon Strongho